        "original_id": "bb5ad9fe-a0c9-5a86-8b8d-a867de83677e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Catuaba\n- Places: Brazil, South America\n- Languages: Guarani language, Paraguayan Guarani\n- Concepts: Tupi–Guarani family, Tupian languages\n- Plants: Erythroxylum, Erythroxylum vacciniifolium\n\nFacts:\n- Guarani, specifically Paraguayan Guarani, is an indigenous language of South America in the Tupi–Guarani family of the Tupian languages.\n- The term Catuaba comes from a Guarani word meaning “what gives strength to the Indian.”\n- Catuaba is used for infusions made from the bark of several trees native to Brazil.\n- Erythroxylum vacciniifolium, also known as Catuaba, is used as an aphrodisiac in Brazilian drinks and herbal medicine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
